# No Hardcoded Strings

All user-facing English copy must live in `lib/strings/app_strings.dart` on the `AppStrings` class. Do not embed display text as string literals inside widget trees or business logic.

## Where Strings Live

```
lib/
└── strings/
    └── app_strings.dart   ← single source of truth (English-only app)
```

## Using Strings in Dart

```dart
// ✅ GOOD
import 'package:omnix/strings/app_strings.dart';

const Text(AppStrings.homePageTitle)
Text(AppStrings.someMessageWithInterpolation(foo)) // use a static method if you need params

// ❌ BAD — never do this in UI
Text('My Devices')
```

For messages that need parameters, add a `static String methodName(...)` on `AppStrings` that returns the formatted sentence.

## Exceptions

Non-display strings (route paths, map keys, log messages, `String.fromEnvironment` in `core/config/app_config.dart`) do **not** need to live in `AppStrings`.
